.if \n[.g] .mso www.tmac
.TH SDL_FOURCC 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_FOURCC \- Define a four character code as a
.BR Uint32 .

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_FOURCC(A, B, C, D) \(rs
.BI "    ((SDL_static_cast(Uint32, SDL_static_cast(Uint8, (A))) << 0) | \(rs
.BI "     (SDL_static_cast(Uint32, SDL_static_cast(Uint8, (B))) << 8) | \(rs
.BI "     (SDL_static_cast(Uint32, SDL_static_cast(Uint8, (C))) << 16) | \(rs
.BI "     (SDL_static_cast(Uint32, SDL_static_cast(Uint8, (D))) << 24))
.fi
.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I A
the first ASCII character\[char46]
.TP
.I B
the second ASCII character\[char46]
.TP
.I C
the third ASCII character\[char46]
.TP
.I D
the fourth ASCII character\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the four characters converted into a
.BR Uint32 ,
one character per-byte\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

